{"title":"1998 IMO Shortlist Problems/A1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Mongolia</i>)\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/b/ecbe2a675e27af0c6111e82c2c8667704a7f1ba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\dotsc, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"11\" /> be positive real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/2/6129ee0a04bf12f2bcc54b7f0b593cc395519fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 + a_2 + \\dotsb + a_n &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"173\" height=\"14\" />.  Prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e09c44a2d4c3eb36975cca0baa5ccf50955ee6d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_1 a_2 \\dotsm a_n \\bigl[ 1- (a_1 + a_2 + \\dotsb + a_n) \\bigr]}{ (a_1 + a_2 + \\dotsb + a_n)(1-a_1)(1-a_2) \\dotsm (1-a_n)} \\le \\frac{1}{n^{n+1}} .\\]\" width=\"441\" height=\"46\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36cfb07e4911e7b4f994b858f3d47604ddbee438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> be the positive real number such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ff69d3da5607e582a83c1b844aaff3dca69997b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1} = 1 - \\sum_{k=1}^n a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"136\" height=\"48\" />.  Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a660c3d5fb1de6c109a5f9c7af92b4cdc3a2059.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_1 a_2 \\dotsm a_n \\bigl[ 1- (a_1 + a_2 + \\dotsb + a_n) \\bigr]}{ (a_1 + a_2 + \\dotsb + a_n)(1-a_1)(1-a_2) \\dotsm (1-a_n)} = \\frac{\\prod_{k=1}^{n+1} a_k} {\\prod_{k=1}^{n+1} \\sum_{j\\neq k} a_j} .\\]\" width=\"513\" height=\"51\" />\nBut by AM-GM, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/e/39e9e53df87af766249d9a829cebb244f8f73504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j\\neq k} a_j \\ge n \\prod_{j\\neq k} a_j^{1/n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"141\" height=\"40\" />.  Hence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/8/528f1271c97425ceb3711d037028d4fbfbff7c3e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\prod_{k=1}^{n+1} a_k}{\\prod_{k=1}^{n+1} \\sum_{j\\neq k} a_j} \\le \\frac{\\prod_{k=1}^{n+1} a_k}{\\prod_{k=1}^{n+1} n \\prod_{j\\neq k} a_j^{1/n}} = \\frac{\\prod_{k=1}^{n+1} a_k}{n^{n+1} \\prod_{k=1}^{n+1} a_j} = \\frac{1}{n^{n+1}},\\]\" width=\"474\" height=\"52\" />\nas desired.  Equality holds when all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> are equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2e982fe34ac21ec1cf77ae10b1c447eb194f5e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Shortlist_Problems\" title=\"1998 IMO Shortlist Problems\">1998 IMO Shortlist Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mathlinks.ro/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=124417#p124417\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017063119\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.024 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 70/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 353/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2559/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.601      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    5.601      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6096:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017063119 and revision id 21672. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}